{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a stitch task (Task #5657) from the cobbler-scaffold code generation pipeline to implement four specific requirements from srd004-ts (the `ts` timestamp utility) in the go-unix-utils project. The requirements are:\n   - **R9.2**: Add differential test cases covering: default format, custom strftime format, -s mode, -i mode, -m mode (with monotonic normalization), multi-line stdin, empty stdin, and partial last line (no trailing newline).\n   - **R10.1**: When `-r` and a format string are both given, convert matched timestamps to the specified strftime format rather than to a relative age string.\n   - **R10.2**: In `-r` mode, lines with no recognizable timestamp must be passed through unchanged.\n   - **R10.3**: `-r` is mutually exclusive with `-i` and `-s`; passing both must print a usage error to stderr and exit non-zero.\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/ts/main.go` (implementation) and `cmd/ts/ts_test.go` (tests).\n   Acceptance criteria: AC1-AC4 require all four requirements implemented, `go build` succeeds, `go test` passes (or skips gracefully), `go vet` reports no issues.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Differential testing**: Go binary output is compared byte-for-byte against Homebrew reference binary (`ts` from moreutils)\n   - **pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests**: Framework for running differential tests with `DiffTest` structs\n   - **testutils.TimestampNormalizer**: Replaces wall-clock timestamps with fixed placeholders for stable comparisons\n   - **strftime formatting**: ts uses strftime-style format strings including subsecond extensions (%.S, %.s, %.T)\n   - **Relative time mode (-r)**: Scans input for timestamp patterns and replaces with relative age strings or reformats via strftime\n   - **Monotonic clock mode (-m)**: Uses CLOCK_MONOTONIC for timestamps that don't jump on wall-clock adjustments\n   - **Incremental (-i) and elapsed (-s) modes**: Show time between lines or time since start\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: Must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` in main()\n   - **Execution constitution rules**: 40-line function limit, 500-line file limit, copyright headers, DRY enforcement, no git commands\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd004-ts.yaml** (READ in full)\n     - Critical for understanding what R9.2, R10.1, R10.2, R10.3 require\n     - R9.2 (line 120-124): Test coverage requirements for differential tests\n     - R10.1 (line 92-93): `-r` with format string converts timestamps to strftime format instead of relative string\n     - R10.2 (line 94): Lines without recognizable timestamps pass through unchanged in `-r` mode\n     - R10.3 (line 95-96): `-r` mutually exclusive with `-i` and `-s`\n     - R6.1-R6.2 (line 84-87): `-r` mode scans for timestamp patterns (syslog, ISO-8601, RFC 2822, lastlog) and replaces with relative age\n     - Non-goals (line 126-130): No colorization, no file reading, no localized date parsing, no --help/--version\n   \n   - **cmd/ts/main.go** (NOT YET READ - needs to be read to understand existing implementation)\n   - **cmd/ts/ts_test.go** (NOT YET READ - needs to be read to understand existing tests)\n   \n   - **Package contracts** (from prompt context):\n     - `testutils.DiffTest`: `type DiffTest struct { Name string; Args []string; Stdin []byte; Env []string; WorkDir string; ExitCode int; Normalize []NormalizeFunc; ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte }`\n     - `testutils.RunDiffTests`: `func RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)`\n     - `testutils.TimestampNormalizer`: `var TimestampNormalizer NormalizeFunc` - used for normalizing wall-clock timestamps\n     - `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler`: `func InstallSIGPIPEHandl